# Line endings for the files where a carriage return is a defect rather than a
# formatting preference.
#
# The repository stores LF, and git hands a Windows checkout CRLF unless a file
# here says otherwise. shellcheck reports SC1017 on every line of a script
# carrying a carriage return, so without these rules the local battery and the
# hosted one read different bytes and reach different answers.
#
# Scoped to shell scripts and git hooks on purpose. A blanket `* text=auto`
# renormalizes files this repository compares byte for byte, and the workspace
# gate asserts that each package's LICENSE and NOTICE match the root copy
# exactly.

*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/hooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
scripts/hooks/commit-msg text eol=lf
scripts/hooks/post-commit text eol=lf
scripts/hooks/prepare-commit-msg text eol=lf
scripts/hooks/install.sh text eol=lf

# The files this repository compares byte for byte against a published text.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on a Windows checkout, so without these rules git hands
# that checkout a LICENSE with CRLF endings. It reads as the Apache License to
# anybody who opens it and is 11544 bytes rather than the 11358 apache.org
# serves, so VAL-GATE-LIC-001 fails on Windows and passes everywhere else.
#
# `-text` rather than `text eol=lf`: the point is that git performs no
# conversion in either direction, on the way in or the way out. These bytes are
# not this repository's to normalize.
LICENSE -text
NOTICE -text
packages/*/LICENSE -text
packages/*/NOTICE -text
tools/*/LICENSE -text
tools/*/NOTICE -text
